{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795288090,"nonce":"In+Nb6o/Kw9Mk2uexGyLCFBWlSc=","title":"jno.flow: a callable velocity on a symbolic pytree state sees one slot, not a pytree","message":"A callable velocity gets one slot per leaf when x0 is a concrete pytree, so x[\"p\"] works eagerly. When x0 is symbolic its structure is unknown at trace time and the state is a single slot; x[\"p\"] then becomes a getitem with key (\"p\",), which fails on a dict at evaluation. Reproduce: jno.flow(lambda x, t: {\"p\": -x[\"p\"]}, \u003csymbolic expression evaluating to a dict\u003e, time=(0, 1, 3)) inside jno.core. A model velocity is unaffected (it takes the state whole). Fix options: infer the state structure with an eval_shape of x0 at build time, or make getitem on a slot a dict lookup.","files":null}]}